[[:db/retract 17592186417735 :answer-field/choices 17592186417712] [:db/retract 17592186417735 :answer-field/choices 17592186417722] [:db/retract 17592186417735 :answer-field/choices 17592186417723] [:db/retract 17592186417735 :answer-field/choices 17592186417724] [:db/retract 17592186417735 :answer-field/choices 17592186417726] [:db/retract 17592186316831 :answer-field/choices 17592186315616] [:db/retract 17592186316831 :answer-field/choices 17592186315969] [:db/retract 17592186316831 :answer-field/choices 17592186316023] [:db/retract 17592186316831 :answer-field/choices 17592186315482] [:db/retract 17592186316831 :answer-field/choices 17592186315660] {:db/id 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d6084cfc-eb77-5ae0-9ec3-a6e87e13ee7f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119624 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119625 :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](images/db/db533ede6312d49204e619379dfff639c0871f37ee997ce152ec35bd64105926.svg) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247208 :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6084cfc-eb77-5ae0-9ec3-a6e87e13ee7f" :question/id #uuid "d6084cfc-eb77-5ae0-9ec3-a6e87e13ee7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34980" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}] & =0 \\\\ -7k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for this equation, we obtain $k=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b1195de-a391-5f4a-ba01-152a7cff1406"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b1195de-a391-5f4a-ba01-152a7cff1406" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b1195de-a391-5f4a-ba01-152a7cff1406" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b2f74fd-3217-5473-9e5d-cc531fb68341" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c378093-8041-5762-8640-d5a40681b948" "answer-cceb993a-7fdf-519c-8422-5d552bf54f8f" "answer-5b2f74fd-3217-5473-9e5d-cc531fb68341" "answer-45a35883-74f9-50df-a12a-cf22366812d0" "answer-92e9ac83-d31a-5747-bd54-27c5176de395"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c378093-8041-5762-8640-d5a40681b948" :answer/id #uuid "5c378093-8041-5762-8640-d5a40681b948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cceb993a-7fdf-519c-8422-5d552bf54f8f" :answer/id #uuid "cceb993a-7fdf-519c-8422-5d552bf54f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b2f74fd-3217-5473-9e5d-cc531fb68341" :answer/id #uuid "5b2f74fd-3217-5473-9e5d-cc531fb68341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45a35883-74f9-50df-a12a-cf22366812d0" :answer/id #uuid "45a35883-74f9-50df-a12a-cf22366812d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92e9ac83-d31a-5747-bd54-27c5176de395" :answer/id #uuid "92e9ac83-d31a-5747-bd54-27c5176de395" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186417740 :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186417735 :answer-field/correct "answer-78246ec8-609c-551f-b0ac-0dadda339bf8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3181278-1876-5206-9569-f7c580389091" "answer-78246ec8-609c-551f-b0ac-0dadda339bf8" "answer-1dea2883-7aed-50ab-88db-338d6b05d1d2" "answer-6d08ac3a-bf71-57e5-86bb-45513f396dce" "answer-bcdbf8dd-4179-511e-ac05-173b55d1fa27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3181278-1876-5206-9569-f7c580389091" :answer/id #uuid "a3181278-1876-5206-9569-f7c580389091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78246ec8-609c-551f-b0ac-0dadda339bf8" :answer/id #uuid "78246ec8-609c-551f-b0ac-0dadda339bf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dea2883-7aed-50ab-88db-338d6b05d1d2" :answer/id #uuid "1dea2883-7aed-50ab-88db-338d6b05d1d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d08ac3a-bf71-57e5-86bb-45513f396dce" :answer/id #uuid "6d08ac3a-bf71-57e5-86bb-45513f396dce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcdbf8dd-4179-511e-ac05-173b55d1fa27" :answer/id #uuid "bcdbf8dd-4179-511e-ac05-173b55d1fa27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317454 :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316831 :answer-field/correct "answer-bd56a073-7763-5f3e-8627-e620cdb34e7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd56a073-7763-5f3e-8627-e620cdb34e7b" "answer-9e92c0f2-12f6-52e4-bc39-5f630e281daf" "answer-6572e448-2a1b-54fa-b7eb-b164a363dfcd" "answer-b0b063f1-874e-516d-844c-6910584fd9fa" "answer-77ade1d1-f580-5223-b0a2-1bf51cbff285"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd56a073-7763-5f3e-8627-e620cdb34e7b" :answer/id #uuid "bd56a073-7763-5f3e-8627-e620cdb34e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e92c0f2-12f6-52e4-bc39-5f630e281daf" :answer/id #uuid "9e92c0f2-12f6-52e4-bc39-5f630e281daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6572e448-2a1b-54fa-b7eb-b164a363dfcd" :answer/id #uuid "6572e448-2a1b-54fa-b7eb-b164a363dfcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0b063f1-874e-516d-844c-6910584fd9fa" :answer/id #uuid "b0b063f1-874e-516d-844c-6910584fd9fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77ade1d1-f580-5223-b0a2-1bf51cbff285" :answer/id #uuid "77ade1d1-f580-5223-b0a2-1bf51cbff285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121063 :tutorial/content "Let's again consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/8f/8fa69630c71d5106ed04a5281681992687174891b1c0978521c12e914cb3a0b0.svg)\n\nTo find an expression for the null space using set-builder notation, we need to find all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Let's start by considering the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ and finding its reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,0] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st column). The second column is not a pivot column.\n\nNow, we convert the reduced matrix back into a system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $\\color{blue}x_1$ is a basic variable (it corresponds to the pivot column), while $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable (it corresponds to the non-pivot column). Because there is a free variable, the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions. \n\nFrom the first equation we get ${\\color{blue}x_1}=-3{\\color{red}x_2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is\n![](images/8c/8c5541adb07cb58136d71fb4e3218981f1717b929f22acbe55d133cd0c395870.svg)\n\n**Note:** It is not necessary to consider the full augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ since the last column won't be changed during the process of reduction. Really, we just need to find the reduced row echelon form of the matrix $A$ and then set up the corresponding system." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}]
